{
  "messages": [
    {
      "time": "09:15",
      "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
      "role": "Field Engineer",
      "text": "Moi Erkki, I'm at site OULU-11 working on TRN-087. I just replaced the SFP because of some CRC errors, and the link is up now with good RX power, but traffic counters are staying at zero."
    },
    {
      "time": "09:17",
      "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
      "role": "Field Engineer",
      "text": "By the way TRN-034 had a dispatch last week too, different thing though. But yeah, this TRN-087 is acting weird now."
    },
    {
      "time": "09:20",
      "author": "Erkki Expert",
      "role": "Network Expert",
      "text": "Moi Veikko! Let me check the node from here. Yes, I see the link state is up and optical levels look totally normal."
    },
    {
      "time": "09:22",
      "author": "Erkki Expert",
      "role": "Network Expert",
      "text": "This is a known quirk with these units. When the link is up and optics are normal after an SFP change but counters stay at zero, you should just disable the interface, wait a bit, and then enable it again. Don't reboot the unit and don't swap the SFP again."
    },
    {
      "time": "09:25",
      "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
      "role": "Field Engineer",
      "text": "Ah okay, good to know. I was just about to swap the SFP again to be sure, glad I asked first. Let me try disabling the port now."
    },
    {
      "time": "09:27",
      "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
      "role": "Field Engineer",
      "text": "Okay, port is disabled. Waiting for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "time": "09:29",
      "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
      "role": "Field Engineer",
      "text": "Now enabled it back. Hey, the traffic counters started incrementing immediately! :)"
    },
    {
      "time": "09:32",
      "author": "Erkki Expert",
      "role": "Network Expert",
      "text": "Excellent, traffic is flowing normally now. That bounce always clears the stuck buffer on TRN-087 after a hot-swap. Good job!"
    }
  ]
}
